{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-034_e32ea33b2de3\tUniProtKB:P0DOV5\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47897\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tPMID:26195800|PMID:39840830|UniProtKB:P0DOV5\tFunctional protein/activity relation, not monomer sufficiency. The 2025 recombinant SQ1 enzyme is tetrameric in solution and crystals. Minor NADP activity and trace G6P activity are assay-dependent side activities outside the native NAD-dependent step.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV5\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"SQ1 IMG0090 was cloned and purified from recombinant E. coli; it oxidized SQ to SGL with a strong NAD+ preference. Whole-pathway reconstitution used the purified protein.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s4\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[2]; Figure 4B; SI Heterologous Overproduction and Purification of His-Tagged Proteins\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:39840830\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The codon-harmonized SQ1 SQDH construct has a tetrameric solution state by SEC-MALLS (~119 kDa versus ~28 kDa monomer), consistent with its crystals. The published untagged sequence equals P0DOV5.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s2-2\\\"\"]/p[1]; Figure 4; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5-2\\\"\"]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5-3\\\"\"]/p[1]\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:39840830\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Under the 2025 kinetic conditions, NAD+ was favored over NADP+ by about 10^6 in catalytic efficiency, and very weak G6P turnover was detectable at high enzyme concentration; the 2015 negative assay is condition-specific.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s2-1\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s2-1\\\"\"]/p[2]; Table 1\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article including SI methods, tables and figure legends in publisher-deposited PMC HTML; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Entner-Doudoroff pathway for sulfoquinovose degradation in Pseudomonas putida SQ1.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:39840830\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"d3059313116aeac892709ea5a759bc1900fc4f47e8d021ff965a5a3c557f36b3\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2025 full primary PMC HTML, including complete construct sequences and Methods; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Structure, kinetics, and mechanism of Pseudomonas putida sulfoquinovose dehydrogenase, the first enzyme in the sulfoglycolytic Entner-Doudoroff pathway.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12133307/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV5\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"c39828a60a1c3ba040a95bd392a9d1514fa8b2134cf5d1bc2fa7ae475b9ebd24\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Complete reviewed entry JSON retrieved 2026-10-11; entry version 25, sequence version 1; last annotation 2026-09-02\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Sulfoquinovose 1-dehydrogenase\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0DOV5.json\"\"}]\"\n"},"line_number":8907,"absolute_offset":10448852,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":2292,"end":2308},{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":2846,"end":2862}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-035_84fb7a58a7b5\tUniProtKB:P0DOV6\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47909\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tPMID:26195800|UniProtKB:P0DOV6\tFunctional activity assignment. Divalent-metal binding below is a reviewed similarity inference, not an SQ1 metal-titration measurement. No physical monomer or oligomer state is inferred from the native MONOMER frame name.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV6\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0091 converted SGL to SG in sequential reconstitution. Minor spontaneous hydrolysis was also observed before lactonase addition; it does not replace the enzyme-supported native step.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[2]; Figure 4B-C\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article including SI methods, tables and figure legends in publisher-deposited PMC HTML; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Entner-Doudoroff pathway for sulfoquinovose degradation in Pseudomonas putida SQ1.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV6\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"c2c78a34870f5edbf56ec4d4ee56fe715cdebad570050ffcb8e159b87a378ab9\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Complete reviewed entry JSON retrieved 2026-10-11; entry version 21, sequence version 1; last annotation 2026-06-10\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"6-deoxy-6-sulfogluconolactonase\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0DOV6.json\"\"}]\"\n"},"line_number":8908,"absolute_offset":10452175,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":1476,"end":1492}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-036_8504cbfea27d\tUniProtKB:P0DOV7\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47913\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tPMID:26195800|UniProtKB:P0DOV7\tFunctional activity assignment; current reviewed homodimer and one [4Fe-4S] cluster annotations are inferred by similarity to Q1JUQ1, not directly measured SQ1 assembly or cluster occupancy.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV7\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0089 converted SG to KDSG in the sequential reconstitution; its preparation also contained C-terminally truncated products identified by peptide fingerprinting.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[2]; Figure 4C-D; Figure S4 legend\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV7\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The homodimer annotation is ECO:0000250 inference from Q1JUQ1. It is not direct experimental assembly evidence for SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/3/texts/0\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article including SI methods, tables and figure legends in publisher-deposited PMC HTML; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Entner-Doudoroff pathway for sulfoquinovose degradation in Pseudomonas putida SQ1.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV7\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"0566981bd12cca55a07e8a7bb627a5798bbb41859b6168e9aaf2a2f6e6e02ee8\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Complete reviewed entry JSON retrieved 2026-10-11; entry version 26, sequence version 1; last annotation 2026-09-02\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-gluconate dehydratase\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0DOV7.json\"\"}]\"\n"},"line_number":8909,"absolute_offset":10454185,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Entner-Doudoroff"},"start":1674,"end":1690}]}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"./pages/downloads/edges.tsv"},"lines":{"text":"pathwaymech:MetaCyc_PWY-7722_sulfoed-edge-037_3022be361192\tUniProtKB:P0DOV8\tpathwaymech:enables\tRHEA:47925\tbiolink:Association\tinfores:pathwaymech\tknowledge_assertion\tmanual_validation_of_automated_agent\tNCBIProtein:KHL76360.1|PMID:26195800|PMID:41830472|UniProtKB:P0DOV8\tFunctional assignment of the reviewed SQ1 gene product. The 2015 cloned IMG00100 gene uses an upstream start relative to the current GenBank annotation at the same locus. Native prose has stale R-SLA/family annotations; current native reaction and Rhea/UniProt chemistry select S-SLA. No monomer sufficiency is asserted.\t\"[{\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"UniProtKB:P0DOV8\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"ECO:0000269, PMID26195800: this reviewed SQ1 gene product is assigned the specified catalytic activity; its cited genomic and experimental references explicitly name strain SQ1.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/comments/1/reaction; /references/0/referenceComments; /references/1/referenceComments\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"Purified recombinant SQ1 IMG0100 cleaved KDSG to SLA and pyruvate. Pyruvate was verified by a positive lactate-dehydrogenase assay and HPLC cochromatography; the SLA assay was not enantiomer-resolved.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[1]; //*[@id=\\\"\"s5\\\"\"]/p[2]; Figure 4D-E\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The cloned IMG00100 used forward primer CACCATGTCCACTGCTGTCACG. All recombinant inserts came from SQ1 chromosomal DNA and were sequence-verified; the paper does not specify current UniProt accessions.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"//*[@id=\\\"\"si8\\\"\"]/p[1]; Table S2, PpSQ1_00100f row\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"NCBIProtein:KHL76360.1\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The original SQ1 protein record locates PpSQ1_00455 at complement(JTCJ01000004.1:18793..19560). This is the current annotated gene call, not a claim that its N terminus equals the longer 2015 construct.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_feature-table/GBFeature[GBFeature_key=\\\"\"source\\\"\"]/GBFeature_quals; /GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_feature-table/GBFeature[GBFeature_key=\\\"\"CDS\\\"\"]/GBFeature_quals; /GBSet/GBSeq/GBSeq_sequence\"\"}, {\"\"reference_id\"\": \"\"PMID:41830472\"\", \"\"source_assertion\"\": \"\"The 2026 P. putida aldolase abstract reports a homohexamer, optimal Co/Mn activity and modest KDPG cross-reactivity. The accessible abstract does not expose its strain or construct sequence; these details are contextual and are not transferred as direct SQ1 assembly/metal assignments.\"\", \"\"source_locator\"\": \"\"/resultList/result[0]/abstractText\"\"}]\"\t\"[{\"\"id\"\": \"\"NCBIProtein:KHL76360.1\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"8736f6a5439a022c10f154cafdeb607f32515739d029ccbfe72020b7bf5165e7\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original accession-version GBSet/GBSeq XML retrieved 2026-10-11; sequence and strain/CDS identity only, automated original functional name not imported\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"SQ1 PpSQ1_00455 protein and genomic CDS annotation\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=protein&id=KHL76360.1&rettype=gb&retmode=xml\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:26195800\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"e82307720415251fbe81a8293ed7078effeb5e268502c5776ce9b30f632e8afc\"\", \"\"source_version\"\": \"\"Original 2015 full primary article including SI methods, tables and figure legends in publisher-deposited PMC HTML; retrieved 2026-10-11\"\", \"\"title\"\": \"\"Entner-Doudoroff pathway for sulfoquinovose degradation in Pseudomonas putida SQ1.\"\", \"\"url\"\": \"\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4534283/?pdf=render\"\"}, {\"\"id\"\": \"\"PMID:41830472\"\", \"\"source_sha256\"\": \"\"bfaee9c036939b4db87a8076aacfcebd894569f3f7a31fab54d5a28b49a3c055\"\", \"\"source_version\"\"